==Russian==

===Etymology===
From a {{bor|ru|trk|-}} language, probably a borrowing of a dative singular form attested in Kipchak languages; compare {{cog|tt|баш||head}}, {{cog|ba|баш|башҡа|lit=head.SG.DAT}}.

Initial (in 17th century) meaning 'head of a large fish' implies an origin related to fish trade in South Russia (e.g. on Volga and Don).

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|башка́}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-башка.ogg}}
* {{audio|ru|LL-Q7737 (rus)-Tatiana Kerbush-башка.wav|a=Saint Petersburg}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|башка́|*}}

# {{lb|ru|colloquial|pejorative}} [[pate]], [[noggin]], [[bonce]] (slang word for [[head]], part of the body)
#: {{ux|ru|[[подумать|Поду́май]] [[свой|свое́й]] '''башко́й''' [[о]] [[последствие|после́дствиях]]!|t=Use your '''noggin''', think of the consequences!}}

